INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:__main__:Prompting GPT
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:
{
    "action": "Given the dire circumstances of being in a barren, rocky plain with severe cold and strong winds, my immediate priority is survival. My most critical needs are shelter, warmth, food, and water. I must conserve energy but also act decisively due to the high danger level associated with exposure and hunger. \n\n1. Shelter: I need to improve the existing shelter made from rocky outcrops. I will use any available materials, such as additional rocks or dry grass, to fortify it against the wind and further insulate it. This will help maintain my body temperature, which is currently below normal. \n\n2. Warmth: With my low energy and body temperature, staying warm is crucial. I will gather any dry grass or other materials that can be used for insulation or as a barrier against the wind. If possible, I will create a small fire for warmth if I can find suitable materials. \n\n3. Water: Since there is no visible water source, I need to focus on identifying potential underground moisture by observing insect activity. My skill in 'Water Source Identification' can guide me to explore areas with increased insect presence for digging or other means of accessing water. \n\n4. Food: With minimal food available, I must rely on any insects I can find, given their slight presence. This will require careful observation and quick action to gather what little nutrition I can. \n\n5. Health Management: I must monitor my injury and illness levels, ensuring they do not worsen. Maintaining my current health status is crucial, given the low immunity and high exposure risks. Resting in the improved shelter should slightly improve my energy and overall health. \n\nThese actions are critical for sustaining myself in this harsh environment, focusing on immediate survival while conserving energy for future challenges."
}

